The Alpha “alignment check” routes misaligned accesses to the generic helper; it does not reject them. Also, `ofs` comes from address bits 5–6 after the shift, so width alignment would not eliminate any of the 16 lane/length pairs. The earlier assessment’s qualification still matters: most downstream failures already zero the byte, so the uninitialized-read claim needs a narrower statement.
