regress\artifacts\alphaswpctxptbr\grok_witness_20260907.txt:1:I'll treat this as a premise audit, not a ratification. First I'll confirm the live repo state, then read the PALcode and Alpha dispatch path myself.HEAD matches the checkpoint. Next I’ll read the swpctx handler and Alpha PAL dispatch myself instead of taking the brief’s excerpts as given.The assignment bug is in source. I’ll read the full handler, `call_pal` dispatch, and how Alpha machines enter PAL so Q1/Q2 rest on the code, not the excerpt.An Alpha harness probe already exists and names this defect. I’ll read it, then check translation and PAL gating against the source rather than the probe’s comments.**VERDICT: YES, a rung-3 witness is buildable on the three constructing Alpha machines — but the proposed “no MMU at all, two `swpctx`, read `A+16`” design is unsound as written if `A.flags` is nonzero. After the first switch, `apcb_ptbr` *is* the flags word, the identity map dies, and the second `call_pal` (and the save that is supposed to publish the bug) can fail to land or can `exit(1)` the host. Use K0SEG for code and both PCBs, or keep `flags==0` and accept a weaker oracle. The one-token fix is not a PAL convention; it is a copy-paste of the previous LHS.**
