regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\ollama_kimi.txt:47:- READ-stated (bodies not inlined): exits in `lca_pci_conf`, `lca_isa`, `lca_interrupt_assert/deassert`. Settling fact: those function bodies.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\ollama_kimi.txt:55:Two facts settle it, both cheap: (1) which machine file under `GXEMUL-SEC/src/` instantiates `dev_lca` and at what physical base (one grep for the init call); (2) the values of `LCA_IOC_BASE` and `LCA_IOC_W_MASK0` (the header). If both exist, a rung-3 debugger store of any value `!= 0x700000` to `machine_base + (LCA_IOC_W_MASK0 - LCA_IOC_BASE)` reaches the arm through real decode; the probe need not match any real guest's value stream, so envelope violation is free. If no machine instantiates the device, it is documented-only.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\ollama_glm.txt:37:- **NOT CHECKABLE:** STAT0/STAT1 having no case (no enum inlined; settling fact: the `LCA_IOC_*` enum vs the case list); the exits in `lca_pci_conf`, `lca_isa`, and the interrupt functions (not inlined — asserted only).
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\ollama_glm.txt:42:**NOT CHECKABLE from the packet.** No machine list, no `LCA_IOC_BASE` value, no address map, no debugger capability is inlined. Three facts settle it: the numeric value of `LCA_IOC_BASE`; the bus address at which the in-tree Alpha machine registers the IOC (wherever `dev_lca` init is called); whether a rung-3 probe can issue a physical store on Alpha. Outside-packet hardware lore, flagged as such and not to be treated as fact: Linux's `core_lca.h` maps IOC_CONF at physical 0x180000000, so *if* the tree wires the IOC at hardware addresses, a store to 0x180000000 plus the per-register offsets reaches the arms. Whether that "if" holds is precisely the grep above.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\ollama_deepseek.txt:17:Yes, that is right. The `default:` arm still diagnoses and exits for both reads and writes; `LCA_IOC_STAT0` and `LCA_IOC_STAT1` have no case; and explicit exits remain in `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_pci_conf)`, `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_isa)`, and the interrupt assert/deassert functions. Nothing else from the packet.
