regress\artifacts\alphaswpctxreg\panel_p1_20260908\grok.txt:1:I'll treat this as a premises check, not a ratification. First I'll read the PAL handler, ABI wrapper, and register conventions against the census you already have.The handler matches the packet. Next I’ll check the ABI wrapper, register numbers, and whether any guest actually calls `swpctx`.Existing notes already flag this as `alphaswpctxreg`. I’ll read those and the Alpha boot/witness material before answering reachability.Census and prior notes are in. I’ll now check PAL docs, alphabook1 boot, and the existing #507 probe so reachability isn’t guessed.Codex already answered this brief; I’ll re-check the census, PAL spec, alphabook1 boot, and the #507 probe instead of adopting that write-up.**VERDICT: `ALPHA_A0` → `ALPHA_V0` is the right one-identifier fix and is sufficient. Keep `med`. Do not clobber `a0`. Do not take the `:296` TODO. A booted OS that consumes `v0` is not established; a rung-3 planted-guest witness on unmodified `alphabook1` is, and that does not make the round documented-only.**
