regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\pass5_panel_20260906_090810\codex.txt:6293:tools/pipeline/ledger.json-28272-    "note": "Closed in the main loop (claude-fable-5-1, author self-review disclosed, badge A) at ecc4d3b, 2026-09-05: the fix shipped with a 46-row detector (23 -> 36 -> 46 across a four-pass repair chain), four kill tables (6, 12 and 22 mutants; the pass-2 and pass-3 escapes each re-measured on the instrument they escaped), gate 14 four times (844/857/867/867 checks), a rung-3 witness 7/13 -> 13/13.  The chain closed on pass 4 with zero floor breaches surviving adjudication; the remaining announce-grid cells are clause (e), written into the contract and filed as pcc2anngrid.  Seat verdicts at the closing pass: close (grok, deepseek, minimax, Fable-with-changes), not-close (codex derived; Opus and kimi measured -- both graded clause (e) on reading); the measurements settled it."
regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\pass5_panel_20260906_090810\codex.txt:6296:tools/pipeline/ledger.json-28275-   "witness": "probe:regress/artifacts/pcc2defaultkill/witness_20260905/defaultkill_witness.py (rung 3: guest st.b/ld.bu at uncased offsets, 7/13 red on the committed build, 13/13 on the fix; liveness + CHIPID + the arm's own message channel); detector:regress/pcc2_default_probe.py (36 rows, gate 14; kill tables regress/artifacts/pcc2defaultkill/killtable_20260905/ (6 mutants, 23-row instrument) + killtable3_20260905/ (12 mutants, 36-row instrument; the six pass-2 escapes also scored 23/23 on the pass-2 instrument))",
regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\pass5_panel_20260906_090810\codex.txt:6297:tools/pipeline/ledger.json:28276:   "state_note": "Filed on pass 2; addendum 2026-09-04 (Opus, pass 8): SCCTXIACK 0x25 has no case at all and SCCRXIACK's body runs on reads.  The same ACCEPT shape pcc2widthkills turned on, at a different predicate.  Filed in OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md (dated tail, `### pcc2defaultkill`, line 14290 as of 2026-09-04); this row added 2026-09-04 so the dashboard shows it -- the bug file had it, the ledger did not.  PROMOTED med -> HIGH 2026-09-04 by the fix-review adjudication (Fable 5.1, ranked FIRST; GPT-6 Astra concurs HIGH): the unimplemented offsets are real PCC2 registers the in-tree guest driver writes -- if_ie.c:609 `pcc2_lancirq = ...' (0x2a), :612 `pcc2_lancerrirq' (0x2b), :655 `pcc2_lancerrstat' (0x28), verified by grep in _guest-src-openbsd22 -- and any access to them reaches default: exit(1).  This note first said the cheapest witness was `put b 0xfff4202a, 0' -> host exit: MEASURED FALSE 2026-09-05 (put b never reaches a DM_DEFAULT arm; it survives and prints nothing) -- the witness is a GUEST st.b/ld.bu.  Option set to bring to pass 1: DECLINE + latched announce vs BACKED ACCEPT (the register array already backs every offset and the memcpy read path already serves it) vs FAULT; the READ side dies today too.  RE-BASED 2026-09-05: the Fable design seat found (main loop verified: machine_mvme88k.c:106 `unreadable' at 0xfff46000; if_ie.c:407-409 badpaddr match) that if_ie never attaches on this model, so the driver's PCC2 writes never run; HIGH/FIRST rests on the measured rung-3 witness (guest st.b/ld.bu to IEICR -> exit 1; put b does not reach the arm; 7/13 on the committed build, `regress/artifacts/pcc2defaultkill/witness_20260905/`) and severity.  Pass-1 panel dir _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021751.  PASS-1 PANEL CONVERGED (2026-09-05, panel_20260905_021751 + Opus/Fable): READ side keep the served byte with a latched 'served 0x%02x' announce (it is a default, not a computed value: not member 4); WRITE side MEMBER 3, DECLINE + per-offset latched fatal() (once), NOT backed accept (the file's own cased siblings -- SCCERR write-to-clear, the ICRs mask+reassert, the read-only PSCALECNT/SPEED/IACKs -- contradict a blanket store; the addition licence is unmet; it would add a bounded write into pcctwo_reg[] reachable at 0x3d).  The Opus seat BUILT both and measured the 13-row witness 13/13 under BOTH -- disposition-blind -- so the detector owes a read-after-write row in ONE session (measured A 0x0 vs B 0x5a, cased-sibling control 0x0/0x0).  if_ie never attaches (unreadable at 0xfff46000; ie_setupram early return at if_ie.c:561-564); ie0 IS configured in conf/M187 and conf/NFS (the brief's conf grep was wrong).  Unresolved: whether the real PCC2 folds 0x40..0xfff (no MVME manual on disk; fork PCC2_SIZE 0x40 vs guest header 0x1000) -- AT PASS 1; RESOLVED the same night: the manual was fetched at the codex seat's citation and VMESBCP2 Table 6-1 lists $FFF42040-$FFF42FFF as 'PCCchip2 Registers  Repeated' (vmesbcp2.txt:4629), so the fold is the real part's.  Cross-round: fix pcc2c040kill BEFORE any round implements a PCC2 IACK arm (the SCCRXIACK arm runs on READS and the console driver reads it -- routine entry into the C040 path).  PASS-1 PANEL COMPLETE 9/9 (2026-09-05 02:17-03:27; codex via a re-worded copy after a provider refusal; three cloud seats via one re-fire after a concurrent-panel 429).  CONVERGED: fix A (Opus, measured) -- reads keep the served byte with a latched 'served 0x%02x' announce, writes DECLINED with a per-offset latched fatal() (once); no backed accept; IACKs declined; the in-word bytes disclosed as a width matter.  NEW: the alias is DOCUMENTED (Motorola VMESBCP2 Table 6-1, codex); IEERR SCLR reads as zero (a store would fabricate status).  Implementation drafted (fix_pcc2_default.py + a 23-row detector reusing the width probe's session()); ships after the width chain's pass-13 commit.  PASS-2 PANEL COMPLETE 9/9 (2026-09-05 05:56-06:2x; kimi via one re-fire with the packet inline after the pointer form stalled; glm/deepseek via 2 KB mini packets after thinking burns).  VERDICTS: NOT CLOSE (codex, grok, Opus -- Opus MEASURED two 23/23 clean sweeps), GO-WITH-CHANGES provisional (Fable), PASS (kimi, glm, deepseek, minimax).  Count the arguments: six clause-(d)-shaped escapes of the 23-row detector -> L1 class-closure repair in ONE diff (13 rows, 36; data[0] + width in the announces); table 3 = 12 mutants all killed, the six pass-2 ones 23/23 on the pass-2 instrument.  Pass 3 owed on the repair diff.  PASS-3 PANEL (panel_20260905_081718) on the repair diff: close (grok, deepseek, minimax), GO-WITH-CHANGES (Fable), NO-GO (codex: three derived escapes), NOT CLOSE (Opus: SIX MEASURED clean sweeps of the 36-row instrument, one the mirror of its own pass-2 M_O1 -- the #499 shape inside the repair); kimi derived two residuals and exited without a verdict line; glm SEAT FAILURE (thinking burn x2).  Class closure #2 in one diff (fix_pcc2_501c.py): ten rows appended to existing sessions (46), the write-announce value, the latched-path read response, a len-2 read/write, the width label at len 1, one count + one read-back per offset class; M_RELOAD disclosed as unrowable.  Table 4 = 22 mutants, the ten pass-3 ones also scored on the 36-row instrument.  L4s corrected in place: '875 checks' -> the gate's own 857; '23 rows' -> 46 with history; four pass-1 sentences corrected in their own place; the latch-sameoff-3 miss recorded; the tick reason narrowed (COUNT words, while running; signal-driven per timer.c:284 -- Fable's 'between instructions' premise refuted by reading) with the end-span reason added; len 8 disclosed.  Pass 4 owed on the pass-3 repair diff.  PASS-4 PANEL (panel_20260905_112529) on the pass-3 repair diff: CLOSE (grok, deepseek, minimax; Fable GO-WITH-CHANGES); NOT CLOSE (codex derived, Opus MEASURED four 46/46 sweeps and graded them clause (e) itself, kimi MEASURED the len-2 write-announce sweep and graded it (d)); glm DO-NOT-CLOSE-YET on two width-text mirror cells.  All contested cells are len- or offset-scoped and neither operand is body-tested -> clause (e), disclosed with row specs, filed pcc2anngrid.  Zero floor breaches surviving adjudication; the chain CLOSES on this pass.  Records-only corrections applied: the pass-3 write-value repair re-graded L2 (Fable: 'uncommitted -> L1' is the provenance exemption the repair-chain ruling rejects); the two mirror cells added to the exclusions; the contract's '44/44' (a run that never existed) -> 36/36 + 46/46; the stale announce-count sentence reworded.  #501 SHIPPED 2026-09-05: reads keep the served byte (announced as served, with the width), writes declined, per-offset uint64 latch; witness 7/13 -> 13/13.  PASS 2 (panel_20260905_055656) found the 23-row detector BELOW THE FLOOR six ways -- Opus MEASURED two clean sweeps (announce value -> 0; member 6 on the latched path), grok/codex/Fable predicted four -- and codex found the read announce reloading the array after the copy (the tick rewrites counter interiors).  Repaired in ONE diff (L1): data[0] + `(len %d)' in the announces, 13 rows (36), all 43 offsets driven both ways; table 3 = 12 mutants, the six pass-2 ones also measured on the pass-2 instrument.  Pass 3 panel_20260905_112529.  Filed from the round: pcc2iackmodel, pcc2latchinst.",
regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\pass5_panel_20260906_090810\codex.txt:6315:tools/pipeline/ledger.json:28298:     "note": "The adjudicator's hat (Agent).  SHIP: READ member 4-as-served (keep the byte, latched read announce -- gdrom announces reads too), WRITE member 3 (decline + latched announce), NOT member 6 -- the backed-accept warrant is hollow: the cited driver does not run here, and its uses are ICLR/SCLR acknowledge bits a store would retain.  FOUND FIRST (verified by the main loop: machine_mvme88k.c:106, if_ie.c:407-409): if_ie never attaches on this model, so the 'in-tree driver writes these offsets' warrant behind the HIGH/FIRST ranking is a source reading contradicted by the machine description -- re-base on the rung-3 witness + severity (done).  Uniform disposition, no offset-range predicate; disclose the in-word bytes (a width matter, pcc2widecompose) and the IACKs (decline; file ack-modelling on the SCCRXIACK shape).  12 detector rows incl. R3 (write V, read back 0) pinning DECLINE vs BACKED and R10 per-offset announce count; announce shape: a per-offset bitmap, not the 32-bit width word.  Also: SCCRXIACK runs on WRITES too (no writeflag guard) -- pre-existing quirk."
