regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\pass5_panel_20260906_090810\codex.txt:6722:tools/pipeline/ledger.json-29036-   "title": "lunaabsentcpu  dev_luna88k.c reassert_interrupts() calls the NULL interrupt callback of an UNCONFIGURED cpu slot: on the default one-cpu luna-88k two ordinary guest word stores (INT_ST_MASK1 then SOFT_INT1) kill the emulator process with SIGSEGV -- MEASURED, rung 3",
regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\pass5_panel_20260906_090810\codex.txt:6729:tools/pipeline/ledger.json:29043:   "note": "DEFECT, HIGH -- MEASURED (rung 3).  dev_luna88k.c: reassert_interrupts() (anchor `static void reassert_interrupts') walks `for (cpu = 0; cpu < MAX_CPUS; cpu++)' and calls INTERRUPT_ASSERT(d->cpu_irq[cpu]) -- interrupt.h expands that to a direct call through `.interrupt_assert', no NULL check -- while DEVINIT connects cpu_irq[1..3] only under `if (devinit->machine->ncpus >= 2/3/4)' and memset()s the device to zero.  The INT_ST_MASK0-3 store arm (anchor `case INT_ST_MASK0:') does `d->interrupt_enable[cpunr] = idata; reassert_interrupts(d);' with NO ncpus check, and the SOFT_INT0-3 arm sets a per-slot pending bit and calls reassert synchronously.  On the default ONE-cpu luna-88k two ordinary guest word stores -- 0xfc000000 -> 0x65000004 (INT_ST_MASK1), then 1 -> 0x69000004 (SOFT_INT1) -- call a NULL function pointer: the emulator process dies with SIGSEGV, no diagnostic.  WITNESS: _scratchpad/lunaabs/luna_absentcpu_probe.py on the HEAD binary /tmp/gxopus501p4 (dev_luna88k.c cmp-equal to git HEAD 83df95c), committed unmodified `-e luna-88k', cold debugger: C1 RAM liveness OK, C2 device signature OK (MASK0 >>8), A1 the SAME two stores on the CONNECTED slot 0 SURVIVE (attribution), A2 the MASK1 store alone SURVIVES (readback 0x00fc0000: stored as-is), W1 SOFT_INT1 store: HOST DIED signal 11.  LUNA_ABSENTCPU_WITNESS=PRE_FIX_SYMPTOM, 1.4 s; log regress/artifacts/lunaabsentcpu/witness_head_20260905_2130.out, probe as run beside it.  Pre-existing upstream (the loop and the connect guards are 0.7.0 code); #438 removed the exit(1) on low bits in the SAME arm; its probe's D4 row stores 0x84000100 to MASK1 (bits 31, 26, 8 -- bit 26 SET, slot 1 ARMED for the rest of that session) and could not see this only because a cold debugger has nothing pending and the probe never stores SOFT_INT1 (an earlier wording here said 'bit 26 CLEAR'; corrected by the batch-7 Fable adjudication, which also notes that ANY device interrupt after the arming store kills the host on a running guest).  OPTION SET -- batch-7 Fable adjudication RULING (2026-09-05 ~22:40): (a) ALONE -- bound the reassert loop to `d->ncpus' captured at DEVINIT (house idiom dev_mp.c:134/:191 and this file's own RESET_CPU_ALL arm `i < cpu->machine->ncpus'); (b) declining stores to absent slots is REJECTED for this round (an unsourced board-model claim, changes guest-visible readback, reddens two shipped es438 rows D4/E2) and FILED as the question row lunaabsentmaskdecl; (c) a no-op connection fabricates plumbing with no in-tree idiom; (e) a NULL check guards the symptom.  Detector: W1 kill row + the connected-slot control + a `-n 2' ACCEPT row whose channel is cpu 1 ASSERTING (irq_asserted / vector entry), not survival; PRETABLE mutants `cpu <= d->ncpus', ncpus never assigned (slot 0 never asserted: the boot gate reds), `ncpus = 1' hardcoded.  Wire luna_absentcpu_probe.py into gate_m88k_rounding.sh.  Also owed in that round: es438cells (MASK2/MASK3 readback rows).  Ranked HIGH: guest-reachable process death by an ordinary instruction on the machine the project boots (precedent: pcc2defaultkill, m88kexcdeliver ranked on reachability, not on a known driver doing it).  Provenance: retrospective batch 7 -- GPT-6 Astra (codex, max effort, read-only) predicted it from the source ('interrupt delivery can still reach an unconnected CPU callback'); the main loop built and ran the witness the same evening; Fable 5.1 adjudication of batch 7 in flight.  The fix round runs the full nine-seat panel.",
regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\pass5_panel_20260906_090810\codex.txt:6742:tools/pipeline/ledger.json:29056:   "note": "DEFECT, MEDIUM -- split from m88kexcdeliver because faithful delivery needs the FP exception registers FPHS1/FPLS1/FPHS2/FPLS2/FPPT/FPRH/FPRL/FPIT (MC88100 UM Fig 6-1, mc88100.txt:8486-8514, sec 6.8.1), which the fork never writes (grep -c 'FPHS1\\|FPLS1\\|FPPT' src/cpus/*.c = 0); the FPU-disabled case (sec 6.8.4.1, :10324) needs only EPSR.SFD1.  FPECR is already set at the raise sites (X(fdiv_sss) sets FDVZ).  Witness: rung-3 FP-divide-by-zero or FP-with-SFD1-set probe on testm88k; pre-fix `unimplemented vector=0x072' and the machine stops.  Same fallback as m88kexcdeliver (cpu_m88k.c, anchor `vector < M88K_EXCEPTION_USER_TRAPS_START && !implemented'), pre-existing upstream.  Rank below m88kexcdeliver.  Provenance: retrospective re-check (owner directive 2026-09-04) batch 2 -- GPT-6 Astra (codex, max effort) read-only review, adjudicated by Fable 5.1; artifacts regress/artifacts/retro_20260905/batch2_m88k/ (astra_batch2.txt, fable_adj_batch2.md).  The other seven panel seats were DELIBERATELY NOT FIRED on the retrospective (owner scope); the fix round runs the full nine-seat panel.",
