regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\pass3_panel_20260905_220902\codex.txt:2371:GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json:28773:   "note": "DEFECT, MEDIUM -- split from m88kexcdeliver because faithful delivery needs the FP exception registers FPHS1/FPLS1/FPHS2/FPLS2/FPPT/FPRH/FPRL/FPIT (MC88100 UM Fig 6-1, mc88100.txt:8486-8514, sec 6.8.1), which the fork never writes (grep -c 'FPHS1\\|FPLS1\\|FPPT' src/cpus/*.c = 0); the FPU-disabled case (sec 6.8.4.1, :10324) needs only EPSR.SFD1.  FPECR is already set at the raise sites (X(fdiv_sss) sets FDVZ).  Witness: rung-3 FP-divide-by-zero or FP-with-SFD1-set probe on testm88k; pre-fix `unimplemented vector=0x072' and the machine stops.  Same fallback as m88kexcdeliver (cpu_m88k.c, anchor `vector < M88K_EXCEPTION_USER_TRAPS_START && !implemented'), pre-existing upstream.  Rank below m88kexcdeliver.  Provenance: retrospective re-check (owner directive 2026-09-04) batch 2 -- GPT-6 Astra (codex, max effort) read-only review, adjudicated by Fable 5.1; artifacts regress/artifacts/retro_20260905/batch2_m88k/ (astra_batch2.txt, fable_adj_batch2.md).  The other seven panel seats were DELIBERATELY NOT FIRED on the retrospective (owner scope); the fix round runs the full nine-seat panel.",
