regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\fable_adj_batch3a.md:45:(b) Witness: rung-3 IS available. `evbmips -e maltabe` with an ATAPI image (`-d c:`), a guest program (the `wdcringambig` witness already drove the wdc through the committed piix4_ide path on `-e malta` in 34 MIPS instructions): stage the 12-byte INQUIRY CDB with allocation length 37 through six 16-bit data-port stores, then nineteen 16-bit loads; pre-fix the 19th load returns `[0x23|…, 0xFF]`-shaped (last byte minus one), post-fix intact. Controls: the identical program on `-e malta` (LE) returns `[v, 0xFF]` through the same decode (liveness); the over-read latch line is the device signature. The differential alternative needs two things: `row_odd_width` must inspect `buf[]` (it checks `atapi_len`/`atapi_received` only), and the `void memory_writemax64` stub must honour byte order — today it always serialises LE regardless of `stub_cpu.byte_order` (and the default `stub_byte_order = 0` is `EMUL_UNDEFINED_ENDIAN`, which exercises the BE arm, as the file's own comment says).
regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\fable_adj_batch3a.md:57:Witness: rung-3 on the existing landisk wdc rig (`wdc_flood_probe.py`'s machinery, `-d c:` ATAPI image) or `maltabe`: stage a READ(10) CDB beyond the image end, or opcode 0xFF; read `wd_status` and `wd_error`. Pre-fix 0x50/0x58 and 0x00; post-fix ERR set and the error register non-zero. Controls: a valid INQUIRY through the same path shows DRQ with ERR clear (liveness); an out-of-range CHS READ on a plain disk shows ABRT (signature RAM cannot produce).
regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\fable_adj_batch3a.md:115:6. Astra's batch line "C/emulator checks were not run" applies to this adjudication too: two DEFECT rows still owe their rung-3 attempt before any edit.
regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\fable_adj_batch3a.md:119:1. **`wdcbeoddtail`** — DEFECT, **MEDIUM** (HIGH if the over-read latch fires under a real driver on `maltabe`). Title: big-endian odd-tail data-port reads subtract one from the last valid payload byte (the empty-ring sentinel is folded into the value). Witness: rung-3, `evbmips -e maltabe` + ATAPI image, INQUIRY-37 CDB then nineteen 16-bit loads; LE control on `-e malta`; over-read line as signature. Option set: mask pops `& 0xff`; return 0 (reds `overread -1`, oracle-correction order); pad odd transfers to an even count (BELIEVED). Detector obligation discharges part of `wdcletwins` (read-side BE arm) and `wdcprobeendian`; the `memory_writemax64` stub must honour byte order first.
regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\fable_adj_batch3a.md:120:2. **`wdcpktstatus`** — DEFECT, **MEDIUM**. Title: a rejected or CHECK-CONDITION ATAPI packet completes with ERR clear; `atapi_st->status` is never consulted; the #416 CHECK CONDITION repair never reached the IDE path (an out-of-range READ(10) is delivered as zeros with success). Witness: rung-3, landisk wdc rig or `maltabe`, READ(10) beyond the image or opcode 0xFF, read `wd_status`/`wd_error`. Option set: ABRT on failure; mirror sense key into bits 7:4 (needs a `sense_key` accessor); no PHASE_DATAIN on CHECK CONDITION. Guest expectation CONFIRMED on disk (OpenBSD 2.2 `atapiconf.c` `atapi_sense(acp, error >> 4, flags)`); register-layout spec conformance BELIEVED.
