regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch2_m88k\fable_adj_batch2.md:16:- **BATCH: DEFECT.** The live defect is the m88k exception-core fallback (`cpu_m88k.c`, anchor `vector < M88K_EXCEPTION_USER_TRAPS_START && !implemented`): six guest-reachable exception classes stop the machine instead of being delivered. It is upstream code neither #323 nor #380 introduced. A measuring seat should build a rung-3 probe (below) and, when fixing, the deliver-through-common-path form.
regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch2_m88k\fable_adj_batch2.md:44:**(b) Witness (rung 3):** a cold-debugger probe on committed `testm88k` or `luna-88k`, exemplars `regress/m88k_idle_probe.py` / `m88k_rounding_probe.py`. Cleanest: a **supervisor-mode divide-by-zero** (no mode switch needed) — plant `divu r2,r3,r0`, point VBR into RAM, breakpoint at VBR+0x40, free-run. Pre-fix HEAD: `unimplemented vector=0x008` and the machine stops. Post-fix: PC == VBR+0x40, SXIP = the faulting instruction | XIP_V, PSR shadow frozen (SFRZ/IND/SFD1/MODE set), machine still running. Add the two controls the ladder requires: a LIVENESS control (a delivered vector that already works, e.g. an INTERRUPT or a returning path) and an ATTRIBUTION control (the same instruction on a non-faulting operand does not vector).
regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch2_m88k\fable_adj_batch2.md:112:1. **`m88kexcdeliver`** — DEFECT, **HIGH**. *m88k exception core halts every guest CPU for six reachable classes (ILLEGAL_INTEGER_DIVIDE, INTEGER_OVERFLOW, PRIVILEGE_VIOLATION, MISALIGNED_ACCESS, UNIMPLEMENTED_OPCODE — the trap-like five) instead of delivering VBR+8·vector.* Pre-existing upstream (`cpu_m88k.c` anchor `vector < M88K_EXCEPTION_USER_TRAPS_START && !implemented`; `git log -L` → import commit only). Witness: rung-3 probe, supervisor `divu r2,r3,r0`, VBR into RAM, breakpoint at VBR+0x40 — pre-fix `unimplemented vector=0x008` + machine stops; post-fix PC==VBR+0x40, SXIP set, running. Fix: `implemented = true` for the five, flow through common path. Witness owed at rung 3 before any edit.
regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch2_m88k\fable_adj_batch2.md:114:2. **`m88kexcsfu1`** — DEFECT, **MEDIUM** (split from 1). *SFU1_PRECISE (vec 114, 58 raise sites) and latent SFU1_IMPRECISE halt instead of delivering VBR+0x390/0x398.* Additionally needs the FP exception registers FPHS1/FPLS1/FPHS2/FPLS2/FPPT/FPRH/FPRL/FPIT (never written today) for faithful delivery; the FPU-disabled case needs only EPSR.SFD1. Witness: rung-3 FP-divide-by-zero or FP-with-SFD1-set probe. Rank below 1.
