55:cannot-read-files line exists because a stalled packet-fed seat is indistinguishable from a
56:quota wall in the output, and this project misdiagnosed that for days.  Verdict-line-first
57:exists because answers get truncated and the verdict is what survives.
58:
59:> ### *** THE ENUMERATE-DO-NOT-REASON LINE, ADDED 2026-08-30 ON FIVE MEASURED INSTANCES IN
60:> ### ONE EVENING -- TWO OF THEM REFUTATIONS OF THIS PROJECT'S OWN FILINGS. ***
61:>
62:> Source-derived arithmetic about *device index expressions* was wrong twice and right three
63:> times that night, and **the discriminator every time was enumeration rather than argument**:
64:>
65:> * `sgilinearoob`'s *"load-bearing HOST memory safety"* was reduced to intra-struct
66:>   corruption by a seat that compiled `offsetof` instead of trusting the derivation;
67:> * **`sgideoob` was WITHDRAWN as a FALSE out-of-bounds** - its analysis skipped the
68:>   `relative_addr &= ~CRIME_DE_START` line sitting immediately above the index computation,
69:>   which halves the range into an array with 512 slots of headroom;
70:> * the TLB-loop OOB, `sgitexindex`'s 81 unreachable cells, and its 3-entry overlap were then
71:>   each **confirmed by walking every reachable address**, after the false one was withdrawn.
72:>
73:> **The failure mode is specific and it is why a general "check the premises" does not catch
74:> *** A THIRD INSTANCE LANDED 2026-08-31, AND IT IS THE FIRST WHERE THE AUTHOR DID ENUMERATE.
75:> *** A brief walked every (access width, offset) pair against a device window -- 8201 declined
76:> accesses, severity escalated -- **omitting the CPU's alignment gate.**  Misaligned accesses
77:> raise ADEL/ADES before `memory_rw` is reached, so a width-w access arrives w-ALIGNED, and on
78:> a page-aligned page-length window the boundary truncation can then never fire at all.  True
79:> answer 6144, and the queue row's original modest claim was right before the brief
80:> "strengthened" it.
81:>
82:> **THREE FILE-READING SEATS REFUTED IT OUTRIGHT.  A FOURTH SEAT -- PACKET-FED -- IDENTIFIED
83:> THE ASSUMPTION, DERIVED BOTH BRANCHES, AND CORRECTLY REFUSED TO SETTLE IT:** *"widths
84:> 3/5/6/7 are guest-reachable only if this fork's MIPS core does not raise AdEL/AdES first.
85:> Under alignment enforcement the counts drop to 6144 declined / 3072 startFlag-set and the
86:> truncation chapter closes entirely."*  That is the correct answer, from the packet alone,
87:> with the undecidable half flagged rather than guessed -- exactly what the packet preamble
88:> asks for.  Two other packet-fed seats reconciled the wrong figure without flagging it.
89:>
90:> > **SO THE RULE IS NOT "SCORE A PACKET-FED AGREEMENT AS ZERO" -- an earlier draft of this
91:> > paragraph said that, and this panel refutes it.  The rule is: a packet-fed seat cannot
92:> > SETTLE a repo fact, so score an UNCONDITIONED agreement as zero -- while a CONDITIONED
93:> > answer, one that names the premise it cannot check, is worth more than an unconditioned
94:> > answer from a seat that could have checked and did not.**
