codex
The design choice is now clear: reject unavailable lanes with a per-instance announcement and `return 0`, and check downstream read failure before packing the byte. On this Alpha path, failure suppresses load-register writeback without delivering a device exception. For the witness portion, I can provide regression assertions, but I can’t supply an unfixed-build guest-trigger recipe.
